From fed5aded8b3c4f26b677164d88966282733ecc4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jean-Michel Hautbois <jeanmichel.hautbois@yoseli.org>
Date: Thu, 4 Dec 2025 11:48:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] m68k: use fast trap for get_thread_area

The Linux kernel for m68k/ColdFire now provides a fast path for
get_thread_area() via TRAP #1, avoiding full syscall overhead.

Instead of:
  move.l #__NR_get_thread_area, %d0
  trap #0  (full syscall with save/restore, signal checks, etc.)

We now use:
  trap #1  (fast trap handler, ~5 instructions in kernel)

This significantly reduces TLS access overhead, which impacts every
errno check and thread-local variable access.

The kernel's fast_get_tp handler (entry.S) reads thread_info->tp_value
and returns it in d0 via RTE, without the full syscall machinery.

Signed-off-by: Jean-Michel Hautbois <jeanmichel.hautbois@yoseli.org>
Upstream: not-submitted, m68k performance optimization
---
 ldso/ldso/m68k/m68k_read_tp.S | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ldso/ldso/m68k/m68k_read_tp.S b/ldso/ldso/m68k/m68k_read_tp.S
index cb5280e67..9165e2dda 100644
--- a/ldso/ldso/m68k/m68k_read_tp.S
+++ b/ldso/ldso/m68k/m68k_read_tp.S
@@ -41,8 +41,7 @@
 # endif
 
 ENTRY (__m68k_read_tp)
-	move.l	#__NR_get_thread_area, %d0
-	trap	#0
+	trap	#1
 	move.l	%d0, %a0
 	rts
 END (__m68k_read_tp)
-- 
